DEPLOYMENT : when the deployment command is executed it creates a deployment which automatically creates replica set ,replica set creates pods,pods downloads & 
runs nginx/given images automatically
  
POD : it is a layer of  abstraction on the top of a container 
     k8s communicates with the pod it does not communicate with the container directly this is the reason even if the underlying containers r not docker the commands
     get executed successfully
  
SERVICE : service is a object that plays a key role in maintaining connection with pods in case of restart ,crash of public ip, the ip adress address gets changed when
          ever it was restarted again in such case service object ensures to maintain connection with  pod without experinecing downtime to costumers by generating the 
          instance with the same old ip address and it also ensures load balancing ,traffic distribution by creating n no.of pods as a service
  
SCALING : scaling  maintains the desired no.of replicas meet the actual no.of replicas always and it ensures to decrease r  increase the no.of replicas depending
          on the load or traffic distributed to a server      
